  "answer": "I have created the professional shipment data Excel file, `shipment_data.xlsx`, incorporating all feedback from the Logistics Analyst and Excel Automation Engineer to ensure the model is audit-ready and analytically deep.\n\n### 1. Data Specification Table\nThe spreadsheet is structured as follows:\n\n| Lane (A) | Loads (B) | Avg Revenue (C) | Total Revenue (D) | Vol Contribution % (E) | Rev Contribution % (F) | Yield Variance (G) |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| Lane A | 12 | $1,850.00 | $22,200.00 | 27.91% | 27.81% | -$5.81 |\n| Lane B | 7 | $2,400.00 | $16,800.00 | 16.28% | 21.05% | +$544.19 |\n| Lane C | 20 | $1,420.00 | $28,400.00 | 46.51% | 35.57% | -$435.81 |\n| Lane D | 4 | $3,100.00 | $12,400.00 | 9.30% | 15.53% | +$1,244.19 |\n| **Total** | **43** | **$1,855.81** | **$79,800.00** | **100.00%** | **100.00%** | **-** |\n\n### 2. Formula Specification Memo\nTo ensure full auditability, the following logic was implemented:\n*   **Total Revenue per Lane (D2:D5):** `=B2*C2` (Volume $\\times$ Rate)\n*   **Total Loads (B6):** `=SUM(B2:B5)`\n*   **Total Revenue (D6):** `=SUM(D2:D5)`\n*   **Weighted Avg Revenue (C6):** `=IFERROR(D6/B6, 0)` (Prevents `#DIV/0!` errors and avoids simple average bias)\n*   **Volume Contribution % (E2:E5):** `=B2/$B$6` (Lane Volume / Total Volume)\n*   **Revenue Contribution % (F2:F5):** `=D2/$D$6` (Lane Revenue / Total Revenue)\n*   **Yield Variance (G2:G5):** `=C2-$C$6` (Identifies if a lane is a \"premium\" or \"discount\" route relative to the portfolio average)\n\n### 3. Professional Formatting Applied\n*   **Typography:** All cells use **Arial** font.\n*   **Emphasis:** Header row and Totals row are **Bolded**.\n*   **Alignment:** \n    *   **Lane:** Left-aligned.\n    *   **Loads:** Center-aligned.\n    *   **Revenue/Percentages:** Right-aligned for decimal consistency.\n*   **Number Formatting:** \n    *   **Currency:** Accounting format (`$#,##0.00`) for Avg Revenue, Total Revenue, and Yield Variance.\n    *   **Percentage:** Percentage format (`0.00%`) for contribution columns.\n*   **Visuals:** Thin borders applied to all cells for a clean, structured financial appearance.\n\nThe final file is available as `shipment_data.xlsx`.",
